<title>ITALY: Reuters Asset Allocation Poll (Italy) - February 4.</title>
<headline>Reuters Asset Allocation Poll (Italy) - February 4.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian banks' and fund managers' investment outlook for February was little changed from last month, but some reduced their total weight on Italian equities in favour of additional liquidity and foreign investments, an Italian Reuters Asset Allocation poll showed.</p>
<p>Averages for division of the total portfolio were influenced this month by the fact that data from one bank which took part in January were not available.</p>
<p>Banco di Sardegna, which uses a longer term timeframe, confirmed the investment preferences it advised in January.</p>
<p>In the last survey respondents were asked to classify Italian floating rate certificates (CCTs) according to their maturity. Italian bank Credito Italiano had incorporated them in medium term bonds and advised investing 34 percent of the total Italian bond portfolio in CCTs. CCTs have now been classified separately.</p>
